ue "153628"} "1,000 metres Time Trial, Men"] "\n" [:option {:value "153684"} "Team Pursuit (4,000 metres), Men"]] [:script {} "$('#same_games_select').change(function(){location.href='/results/' + $('#same_games_select').val();})"]] " | " [:form {:class "form-inline form-inline-header"} [:select {:name "id", :id "other_games_select", :class "form-control"} [:option {:value ""} "In other Games"] "\n" [:option {:value "153101"} "1906"] "\n" [:option {:value "153181"} "1908"] "\n" [:option {:value "153270"} "1920"] "\n" [:option {:value "153334"} "1924"] "\n" [:option {:value "153389"} "1928"] "\n" [:option {:value "153441"} "1932"] "\n" [:option {:value "153499"} "1936"] "\n" [:option {:value "153584"} "1948"] "\n" [:option {:value "153726"} "1956"] "\n" [:option {:value "153826"} "1960"] "\n" [:option {:value "153935"} "1964"] "\n" [:option {:value "154088"} "1968"] "\n" [:option {:value "154231"} "1972"]] [:script {} "$('#other_games_select').change(function(){location.href='/results/' + $('#other_games_select').val();})"]] " | " [:a {:href "/event_names/220"} "Event type"]] [:h1 {:class "event_title"} "Tandem Sprint (2,000 metres), Men" [:small {}]] [:table {:class "biodata"} [:tbody {} [:tr {} [:th {} "Date"] [:td {} "28 – 31 July 1952"]] [:tr {} [:th {} "Status"] [:td {} "Olympic"]] [:tr {} [:th {} "Location"] [:td {} [:a {:href "/venues/374"} "Helsingin Velodromi, Helsinki"]]] [:tr {} [:th {} "Participants"] [:td {} [:a {:href "/events/153659"} "28 from 14 countries"]]]]] [:div {:class "description"} [:p {} "This was the final track event of the 1952 Olympics, the final following shortly after the match sprint final. Fourteen teams started the event. The semi-finals came down to Australia against Italy, and South Africa against France. But South Africa had a walkover, as the French team of " [:a {:href "/athletes/15270"} "Franck le Normand"] " and " [:a {:href "/athletes/17073"} "Robert Vidal"] " could not compete. Le Normand had taken a bad fall in the sprint quarter-final repêchages earlier in the day, and was taken to the hospital. The Australian team was " [:a {:href "/athletes/14010"} "Lionel Cox"] " and " [:a {:href "/athletes/15697"} "Russell Mockridge"] ", who had only ridden together once prior to the Olympics. But they were formidable – Mockridge won the kilometer time trial and Cox was silver medalist in the sprint. The Italian tandem was " [:a {:href "/athletes/16138"} "Cesare Pinarello"] " and " [:a {:href "/athletes/15525"} "Antonio Maspes"] ", also a very formidable team. Pinarello would place second in the sprint at the 1953 World Championships. Maspes turned professional in 1954 and won seven World Championships in the sprint – 1955-56, 1959-62, and 1964. In the semi, Pinarello and Maspes were no match for the Australians, but they won the bronze medal in a walkover, when France could again not come to the mark. The final was a virtual walkover for Cox and Mockridge, who easily won the race over South Africa for the gold medal."] "\n\n" [:p {} "Russell Mockridge turned professional late in 1953. He won several six-day races and managed to finish the 1955 Tour de France. He was unmatched in Australia, winning 12 consecutive national titles. In 1958 he was killed when struck by a bus while riding in the Tour of Gippsland race."] "\n"] [:table {:class "table table-striped"} [:thead {} [:tr {} [:th {} "Pos"] [:th {} "Pair"] [:th {} "NOC"] [:th {} "R1"] [:th {} "R1 Rep"] [:th {} "QF"] [:th {} "SF"] [:th {} "Final"] [:th {}] [:th {}] [:th {}]]] [:tbody {} [:tr {:class "", :style ""} [:td {} "1"] [:td {} [:a {:href "/athletes/14010"} "Lionel Cox"] " / " [:a {:href "/athletes/15697"} "Russell Mockridge"]] [:td {} [:a {:href "/countries/AUS"} [:img {:style "padding-right: 2px; vertical-align: middle", :src "https://olympedia-flags.s3.eu-central-1.amazonaws.com/AUS.png"}] "AUS"]] [:td {} "11.4 (1 h7)"] [:td {} "–"] [:td {} "11.1 (1 h3)"] [:td {} "11.0 (1 h1)"] [:td {} "11.0 (1 h1)"] [:td {} [:span {:class "Gold"} "G